  "lesson": "## Fader open, one click in the middle of every stroke\n\nCrossfader open. Baby-scratch strokes on every eighth for 2 bars; in the middle of each stroke the fader closes and reopens once, quickly. That one click splits each stroke into two sounds, so a single forward-back becomes four notes.\n\nThe flare is the reverse of the chirp: the fader starts open and the cut is in the middle rather than at the end. DJ Times' tutorial builds the two-click flare and the orbit from this, so get the single click exact first. The click must be under 60 ms and dead centre of the stroke; early or late and the two halves are unequal, which the ear hears immediately.\n",
